flagtree (0.6.1-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build one package per backend from packaging/backends.conf: render
    debian/control for the backend being built instead of carrying a single
    hand-written stanza, and take the wheel either from the source build or
    from the index where the backend's delivery workflow published it.
  * Conflict with the virtual python3-flagtree the packages provide, so a new
    backend no longer has to be added to every other backend's Conflicts.
  * Package the backends whose delivery workflow publishes a wheel: amd,
    enflame, hcu, metax, mthreads, ppu, tileir, tsingmicro and xpu, next to
    the nvidia package built from source.
  * Assert only the install for a backend whose compiler module needs its
    vendor SDK or torch while triton is imported (backends.conf: smoke).

 -- FlagOS Contributors <contact@flagos.io>  Tue, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900

flagtree (0.6.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Name the triton module _C/libtriton.so after unpacking the wheel; the
    compile-cache key hashes that file, so kernel compiles failed on the
    installed package.

 -- FlagOS Contributors <contact@flagos.io>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0900

flagtree (0.6.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.6.1.
  * Derive the wheel version from the packaging files (FLAGTREE_WHEEL_VERSION)
    instead of setup.py's hardcoded 0.6.0 fallback.

